    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41307" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτερπ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>pleasing, delightful,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χῶρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ap.</u>
					413
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἃ καὶ λόγῳ.. ἀκούειν οὐκ ἐπιτερπές</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					240e
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Rom.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν πεπραγμένων ἐ. αἱ μνῆμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1166a25
				</span></i>
			 : 
				Sup.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ -έστατα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Democr.
					233
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πῶς, διατίθεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Mus.</u>
					p.84K.
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Num.</u>
				13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>devoted to pleasure</i> (unless =
			<i>pleasant companion</i>), <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				23
			</span></i>.</div>
